    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d430">

                <pb facs="0646" n="558" sameAs="frus:frus1892/pg558"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hirsch to Mr
                            Blaine.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1892-04-18"><hi rendition="#italic">April 18, 1892</hi></date>.
                        (Received May 2.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 431.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In my No. 407 of March 18, 1892, I informed
                    the Department of the seizure of American property and closing of schools at the
                    villages of Tenderiah, etc.</p>
                <p>I have now received from the Rev. Mr. Easson his statement of the case, copy of
                    which I have the honor to inclose. It will be noticed that an attempt at
                    pretended legal proceedings was made in the ease of the Tenderiah property, but
                    I doubt if the Sublime Porte even will claim them to be such legal proceedings
                    as are by the law and the treaties contemplated.</p>
                <p>I have not yet received any reply from the Porte to the note above-mentioned, but
                    shall urge the matter immediately after the Barian festival.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Solomon Hirsch.</hi></signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d430-a1.xml" xpointer="d430-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
